=== Design 1: Implicit null (Java / C pre-Optional) ===
  Null is a valid value of every reference type.
  Dereference crashes at runtime, possibly far from the assignment.
  alice found: 30 years old
  bob lookup -> crash: 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable  (the null dereference)

=== Design 2: Optional type (Kotlin / Swift / Rust Option) ===
  Absence is a separate type; the compiler forces you to unwrap.
  alice: 30 years old
  bob: not found or no age (handled explicitly)

=== Design 3: No null; absence requires a sum type ===
  alice: Some({'age': 30})
  alice age: 30
  bob: Nothing
  bob age: unknown

=== Summary ===
  Design 1 (implicit null): min ceremony, max crash risk
  Design 2 (Optional type): moderate ceremony, compiler-assisted
  Design 3 (no null):       max ceremony, compiler-guaranteed safety
